"culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Digital Realty Trust, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $69.3B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 155% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5523537589250673},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Is Record AI Leasing Building a Bigger Backlog at DLR (NYSE:DLR)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/how-is-record-ai-leasing-building-a-bigger-backlog-at-dlr-nysedlr","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"11,587 Shares in Digital Realty Trust, Inc. $DLR Purchased by Machina Capital S.A.S.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/11587-shares-in-digital-realty-trust-inc-dlr-purchased-by-machina-capital-s-a-s.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794567061.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.962,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Micron, Moody\u2019s, Digital Realty and a Health Care Stock on CNBC\u2019s \u2018Final Trades\u2019","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/11/63243745/micron-moodys-digital-realty-and-a-health-care-stoc